          "802.1X — port-based Network Access Control; requires authentication (often via a RADIUS server) before granting network access, wired or wireless.",
          "Evil twin — a rogue access point mimicking a legitimate SSID to intercept traffic; mitigated with WIDS/WIPS and mutual authentication (802.1X/EAP-TLS).",
